Build succeeds with 0 warnings. Here's a summary of all changes and the Cosmos DB fixes for your separate project:

---

### Changes applied to this project

| # | Breaking Change | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **TFM & packages** | `net8.0` → `net9.0`, EF Core `8.0.0` → `9.0.0` |
| 2 | **`DateTime.UtcNow` in `HasData`** — non-deterministic seed causes "pending model changes" exception at `Migrate()` | Replaced with fixed constant `new DateTime(2024, 1, 1, …)` |
| 3 | **`Migrate()` inside explicit transaction** — now throws | Removed the `ExecutionStrategy` + `BeginTransaction` wrapper; `Migrate()` manages its own transactions |
| 4 | **EF Design package** — SDK 9.0.200+ can't find the assembly | Added `Publish=true` and explicit `IncludeAssets` |

### Cosmos DB project fixes (apply to your separate project)

**5. Discriminator renamed to `$type`** — existing documents use `"Discriminator"`:
```csharp
// In OnModelCreating — preserve old property name
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasDiscriminator<string>("Discriminator");
```

**6. `id` no longer contains discriminator** — breaks `FindAsync` on existing docs:
```csharp
// Preserve old compound id format (e.g. "Product|123")
modelBuilder.Entity<YourEntity>().HasRootDiscriminatorInJsonId(true);
```

**7. Sync I/O now throws** — replace all synchronous calls:
```csharp
// Before (throws in EF Core 9 Cosmos provider)
var items = db.Products.ToList();
db.SaveChanges();

// After
var items = await db.Products.ToListAsync();
await db.SaveChangesAsync();
```
